  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 319 AM EDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nA weak cool front remains forecast to enter the region Wednesday \nnight. This will take 3-5 degrees off high temperatures Thursday \nthrough the weekend, as well as slightly reduce dew points \nespecially north of the Atlanta metro and across the north Georgia\nmountains. Not a massive pattern change, but at least something \nnoticeable for a few days. Heat and humidity will begin to build \nagain across Georgia early next week.\n\nDaily thunderstorm coverage will actually increase for the long-term \nperiod, highest each afternoon and evening. While organized severe \nweather is not currently expected, the stronger storms will continue \nto pose primary risks of lightning, strong wind gusts, and localized \nflash flooding as model forecast soundings show an increasing trend \nin daily PWAT values again back above 2.00 inches. Tropical Storm \nBertha remains expected to track westward toward the northwestern \nGulf, with little to no impact on our local weather.",
